WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.767
-Night, welcome back.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.200
I appreciate this.
-Man, thank you for having me.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.767
-I was so happy to meet
your beautiful wife backstage.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.100
You were telling me
you guys went on a vacation.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.934
And I don't see you as kind of
fanboying out or freaking out,

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:15.000
but you met someone and you kind
of freaked out a little bit.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.334
-Yeah, I mean,
generally speaking, you know,

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.767
kind of -- You know, I've met
so many wonderful people,

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.334
some of them
celebrities and famous people.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.434
And kind of, you know, for me,
the thing that's

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.000
most important
is kind of your --

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.534
the thing that your sacred --
that you consider sacred,

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.133
the thing you're
connecting to as an artist,

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.868
that you keep that precious,
that that's the thing

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.133
that you protect as a musician
or an artist or a painter

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.367
or whatever it is.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.234
And so that's how I judge,
you know, for myself

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:38.934
how much I'm authentic.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.901
And so not often do I
see someone

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:44.200
that I'm, like --
I'm, like, speechless.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.400
And then we were on vacation,
and I got up from the table

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.667
and went down the hall.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.601
And Paul McCartney
bumped into me in the hallway.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:54.400
And I'm like, "Hi, sir.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.467
I'm a..."

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.968
I'm never like this.
And I'm like, "Hi, sir.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.200
I'm -- You know,
I'm M. Night Shyamalan.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.667
I'm a filmmaker. I'm a big fan."

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.634
And he's like, "Oh, wow!
You tell stories. You're great."

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:08.334
And then he was so gracious
and he was so beautiful.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.467
And we sat there in the hall

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.901
and we talked forever
in this hallway.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.033
And he was asking me everything
about filmmaking

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.968
and why and how and what --
you know, how do I tell stories?

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:19.200
And then his grandkids
kept coming up,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.267
and they were like, you know,
"Grandpa, where are you?"

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.734
You know?

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.400
And he was like, "You know, this
is a very important filmmaker."

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.334
He was introducing me
to his grandkids.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.934
-Wow!
-It was so beautiful.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.467
-Do you get that excited,
in general, in life?

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.968
I mean, you're always
very chill when I meet you.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.033
Are you writing another script
or something like that?

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.400
-I am. This morning -- I am.
I'm writing a new script.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.701
I wouldn't come here
until I got my four pages done.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:40.767
And I --
-Is that right?

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.367
-Yeah.
And I got my four pages done.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.968
I was stuck around three pages
and I was like, "Uh-oh.

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.100
I'm not going to make the show."

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.400
-You're gonna cancel on me?

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.067
-Dude, I won't do it.
I won't come. I won't come.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.534
-"I'm not coming on
'Fallon' tonight."

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.267
But you have
the number-1 movie right now.

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.734
You knocked out "Avatar."

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:55.868
-Aw, thanks, man.
-I mean, come on.

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.634
-You've got to celebrate.
-I -- thank you.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:01.634
-"Knock at the Cabin" --
You don't celebrate.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.834
-You know, look, I'll celebrate
the Eagles on Sunday.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.300
-Alright, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:11.167
This is a very young Night right
here with your dad and a camera.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.367
That's a good photo.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:13.801
-That sofa used to have
plastic on it.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:14.901
You know how the parents
used to keep plastic --

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.100
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, of course.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.667
-So that must have been
a real special occasion.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:18.767
they took the plastic off.
-Yeah. Just for the photo.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:19.968
-Yeah, for the photo.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.901
-Then, after the photo,
put the plastic back on.

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:25.000
-My dad is at home.
I'm gonna have him watch this.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.667
And, you know, I think, you
know, now he's very, very old.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:29.868
He had some strokes.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.300
And, you know, he used to be
so excited about

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.200
me being famous and successful,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.934
and now it's just his kid
when I come over.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.534
Like, I think he forgets
all of this.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:39.934
-Is that right?
-Kind of beautiful.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.434
-Aww. And he's just like,
"Yeah, my son's here."

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.868
-"Yeah, my son's here," yeah.
-And how are your kids?

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:44.934
-They're amazing.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:48.634
My daughters
are older and artists.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.601
And one of them is in Ireland.
She's a filmmaker.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.567
She's gonna start her --
do her first film.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.868
-What?!
-Yeah. Amazing.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.033
And the oldest one
is an incredible musician.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.167
And they're touring.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.868
And, just, you know,
amazing, yeah.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.367
-This is cool. Good. I'm happy.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.734
You -- We were --
-Thank you, guys.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:04.968
-We were talking backstage.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.133
You said you were playing
Cards Against Humanity.

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.501
-Yeah.
-Which I love.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.901
We know that game
is a great game.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.067
And this card came up.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.467
You said this is
one of the honors in your life?

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.567
-Well...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.334
-This is one of
the biggest things

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.868
that happened in your life?

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:27.200
Not the number-1 movie.
Don't care.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.567
But if you're a card in
Cards Against Humanity,

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:31.033
you've finally made it?

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.000
-You know, whenever these kind
of pop-culture things happen,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.133
it's very odd.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.167
Like, my mom will
call and be like,

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.968
"You're on 'Wheel of Fortune.'"

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:39.801
And I'm like, "Great, Mom."

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:42.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, I love you, Mom.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:45.901
That's awesome.
-She gets real excited.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.367
We were at my in-laws' house,
and she --

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.701
My sister-in-law picked -- We're
playing Cards Against Humanity.

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:51.901
We've all been drinking.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.567
And then she picks a card
and she starts screaming.

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:54.601
-Yeah.
-"Oh, my God!"

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.868
And I'm like, "Okay, alright."

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.100
She said, "It's you, it's you!"

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.734
And then so I was like,
"Let's play the game.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:03:59.968
Let's keep playing the game."
I'm very competitive.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.133
And so I was like,
"Let's play the game."

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.167
And then we play.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.501
And I give a very funny answer,

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:07.467
like, empirically
the funniest answer.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:08.667
It's just the funniest answer.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:09.934
-Of course.
-And she did not pick me.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:11.167
She picked her husband.
-Yeah, you can't --

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.234
-I didn't even win that round.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.267
-You can't let it all
go to your head.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.400
Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.501
-Everyone's got to
keep you humble. Come on.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:17.767
Let's talk about
"Knock at the Cabin."

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.234
-Yeah.

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:22.033
-It opened Friday, number 1
at the box office this weekend.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:25.234
You recently said
this might be your best film.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.367
Can you set up what it's about?

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.434
-Well, "Knock"
is based on a book,

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:32.534
and it's a about a family
that goes on vacation

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:34.767
into a cabin in the woods.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:37.467
And four strangers
come with weapons.

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.100
They're very menacing.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.367
And they break in.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:43.567
And they tell this family
that they've had

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.133
visions of the end of the world.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.267
And the world
is gonna come to an end,

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.567
and the only way to stop it
is if one of

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:52.334
these three family members
chooses to kill

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.300
one of the other family members.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.901
And if not,
the world comes to an end.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:58.901
-How do you think of
these crazy ideas?

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:03.868
I mean, but you're such
a nice guy, a friendly guy.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.701
I mean, look at this kid.
He's hanging out.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:08.367
He's playing with cameras.
And then he's doing this.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.934
Like, you've gotta kill one
of your family members?

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.267
I mean, oh, my gosh.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.968
-Well, you know, I --
-You just like storytelling.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.167
-Well, I do.

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.834
This one came from a book
that was submitted to me.

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.100
But the next three movies, like,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.767
I know the next three movies
in my head.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.000
And it's very --
It's a very precious thing.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.000
I don't really --
You know, I'm very scared

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.000
that I'm going to stop
coming up with ideas.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.968
And, you know, I was watching
"Signs" the other day,

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.701
which we had a 20th anniversary.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.067
And for a charity thing we did,

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.000
we screened "Signs,"
which is 20 years old.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.467
-Is it 20 years old?
-20 years old.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.734
And I was watching myself
on-screen,

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.300
but also remembering
when I wrote it

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.100
and the ideas I came up with.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.801
And I was just -- how you're not
guaranteed that,

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.567
for 20 years, you're going to
come up with ideas,

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.834
and so I just kind of hoard
the ideas.

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.133
I'm scared, you know,

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.567
that I'm gonna one day wake up
and not be inspired.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.634
-You will never, ever
run out of ideas.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.567
You're M. Night Shyamalan.
Come on, buddy.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:57.968
You're the best.
You can't run out of ideas.

00:05:57.968 --> 00:05:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ever.

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.067
It's never going to happen.
-Thanks.

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.934
-I want to show everyone a clip
from "Knock at the Cabin."

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:05.133
Take a look at this.

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:06.968
-Do you really think that

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:09.100
everything
that happened today...

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.968
everything we've seen...

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:17.634
do you really think
it's all just a coincidence?

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:23.200
-Yes. I think it's all
a coincidence,

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.934
some horrible,
unexplainable coincidence.

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.667
Or it has to be a trick.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.167
I have to believe that.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:32.601
-You already don't believe that.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.968
-Ooh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.434
M. Night Shyamalan.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:40.234
"Knock at the Cabin"
is in theaters now.

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:42.834
We'll be right back with
stand-up from Orlando Leyba.

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:43.968
Stick around, everybody.

